extraction_notes: "Rifts World Book 8: Japan printed 78-79 (cache p079-p080; text layer, page_offset +1), both read against renders. The heading opens mid-column on printed 78 under the chapter''s class contents; the stat block runs from printed 78 into the left column of printed 79 and ends at the Cybernetics paragraph at the foot of printed 79''s right column. Printed 80 (cache p081, the page with corrupt glyphs) was rendered: it opens with the Cyber-Samurai O.C.C. and holds nothing of the Cyberoid, so source_book spans 78-79. || XP: the Cyberoid, Republic Infantrymen column, top right of the Experience Point Tables page (cache p217, folio 216), read off a render: 0 / 1,951 / 3,901 / 8,801 / 17,601 / 35,601 / 50,601 / 70,601 / 95,601 / 125,601 / 175,601 / 225,601 / 275,601 / 325,601 / 375,601. The book prints level 8 as 70,600-95,600, the previous band''s upper bound, so 70,601 is stored. || GROUP: optional, men_of_arms false. The book''s heading groups it under Republic of Japan & Mercenaries, and High-Tech O.C.C.s (printed 78) and its contents list names it Cyberoid/Japanese City Rat O.C.C.; it is the Japanese city rat, a hacker and street character rather than a soldier, so it follows city-rat. No S.D.C., hit points or P.P.E. are printed, so the core values apply. || ATTRIBUTES: none required. An I.Q. under 12 halves the O.C.C. skill bonuses: stored at the full bonus and stated in side_effects and the related note. || SKILLS: Basic Electronics 30+10; Basic Mathematics is Mathematics: Basic 45+20; Language: Japanese & American (+20%) is Language: Native Tongue 98 and Language: Other 50+20; Literacy: Japanese & American (+20%) is Literacy: Native Language 40+20 and Literacy: Other 30+20; Radio: Basic 45+20; Computer Hacking 15+20; Computer Operation 40+20; Computer Repair 25+10; Find Contraband, Weapons & Cybernetics is Find Contraband 26+12; Streetwise 20+12; Pilot Motorcycle is Motorcycles & Snowmobiles 60+10. || HAND TO HAND: Basic Martial Arts/Judo; Aikido for two other O.C.C. skills, Kendo or Karate for three. || RELATED: five, plus one at levels 3, 6, 9 and 12. Military: None, so the category is omitted. Science: Mathematics and chemistry only (+10%). W.P.: any, leaning toward modern weapons (advisory, in the note). || SECONDARY: two at each of levels one, four and ten, from the same list without bonuses. || MONEY: savings 2D4x1000 credits. The 2500-credit salary, the 1D6x1000+10,000 in computer gear and the criminal 1D4x1000 a month are not coin on hand, so they are prose. || EQUIPMENT: the armor and energy weapon are printed for those involved in crime or adventuring; offered as choices over light Japanese armor and ArmaTech/H-Brand energy weapons, with the condition in the note. The several dozen 4.2 meg disks have no catalog row and are named in the hand-held computer note. The motorcycle is unspecified; the two catalog motorcycles are offered. || CYBERNETICS: the book prints a gyro-clock/compass, read as the gyro-compass and clock calendar implants, and a universal headjack and ear implant, plus five of choice, legal or illegal. The headjack has no catalog row and is a stub. The five are an equipment choice over the catalog''s cybernetic implants from this book and Triax; bionic weapons and the Rifts RPG implants are not offered. The optional bionic limb is prose in restrictions."
